# Tracked, time-boxed exceptions for specific CVEs someone has explicitly
# triaged and accepted (not a blanket "no fix yet" bypass - the informational
# scan in the pipeline already surfaces those for visibility without needing
# an entry here). Format: CVE-ID exp:YYYY-MM-DD [reason]
#
# The exp: date is load-bearing: once it passes, Trivy stops honoring the
# entry and the CVE starts hard-blocking the pipeline again, forcing a
# re-triage rather than a silent permanent bypass.
#
# Example (not currently active - no CVEs have been triaged/accepted yet):
# CVE-2024-XXXXX exp:2026-10-01 accepted: no upstream fix, low exploitability in our usage, revisit at expiry
